From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:43:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Keep the first link when a later link fails

A later link of an AP MLD takes the driver instance of the first link in
hostapd_driver_init() and joins the AP MLD only after
hostapd_drv_link_add() succeeds. When that call or the check for driver
MLO support fails, the function returns -1 with the borrowed pointer
still set. The cleanup of the caller then passes it to
hostapd_cleanup_driver() as an instance of its own.

At startup, main() frees the interfaces in order. The cleanup of the
links before the failed one deinitialises the instance, and the cleanup
of the failed link then uses the freed pointer.

Through hostapd_add_iface(), if the failed link has the link ID of the
first link, the cleanup removes that link from the shared instance, or
deinitialises the instance when it has no other link. In the second
case the first link loses its driver instance, and hostapd crashes in
get_capa() when it sets up the next link.

Drop the borrowed instance when the link did not join the AP MLD.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/hostapd/main.c
+++ b/hostapd/main.c
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@ setup_mld:
 		if (!(iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MLO)) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
 				   "MLD: Not supported by the driver");
-			return -1;
+			goto fail_mld;
 		}
 
 		/* Initialize the BSS parameter change to 1 */
@@ -388,13 +388,23 @@ setup_mld:
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
 				   "MLD: Failed to add link %d in MLD %s",
 				   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
-			return -1;
+			goto fail_mld;
 		}
 		hostapd_mld_add_link(hapd);
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	return 0;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+fail_mld:
+	/* A later link only borrowed the driver instance of the first link. */
+	if (h_hapd) {
+		hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+		hapd->interface_added = 0;
+	}
+	return -1;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 }
 
 
